WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.800
Hi, Steve Kaufmann here.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.100
And today I want to talk about
a subject that often comes up.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.290
What is the easiest language to learn?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:08.340
Okay.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.180
Before I get into that, if you enjoy
these videos, please subscribe,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.980
click on the bell for notifications.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.700
If you follow me on a podcast,
uh, please leave a review.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.910
So is there an easier language?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.520
I think here there are both, um,
subjective factors and objective

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.200
factors, which you have to consider.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.070
All right.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:33.705
So I think the most important
consideration is how motivated are you

00:00:33.735 --> 00:00:38.865
to learn the language, uh, because if you
are very motivated, the, the difficulties,

00:00:38.865 --> 00:00:42.795
the objective difficulties, which
I'll get into, will kind of disappear.

00:00:43.215 --> 00:00:48.075
So when it comes to which language is
easiest, you have to begin by saying which

00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:50.565
language am I most motivated to learn?

00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:51.405
All right.

00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:58.545
A second consideration: to what extent
is it easy to find interesting material,

00:00:58.545 --> 00:01:00.525
compelling input in that language?

00:01:01.155 --> 00:01:06.075
Uh, I have to confess that I have had
difficulty with some languages where it

00:01:06.075 --> 00:01:11.565
has been difficult to find compelling
input, Korean, Czech in some ways, uh,

00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:15.945
whereas other languages where there's
lots of content available on the

00:01:15.945 --> 00:01:20.355
internet, especially today, uh, like
Russian and like Spanish, like English.

00:01:20.535 --> 00:01:21.425
It's a lot easier.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.450
Uh, I'm struggling a bit
now with Arabic and Persian.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.080
I have recently found some
really good stuff in Arabic.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:33.390
Um, once I get ahold of some compelling
content, it spurs me on, it influences

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.300
my, my confidence, my enthusiasm.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.300
So, um, obviously a subjective factor then
is how interested are you in the language?

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.960
Uh, can you find compelling
input in  that language?

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.830
Another thing  is confident levels...

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:50.700
confidence level.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.180
If you sort of think you can't or
whatever, if you're, so you're not

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.720
interested or you can't find interesting
content and you think you can't learn it,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.340
it's going to be very difficult for you.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.430
Whereas if you are convinced
that you can do it, this is

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.840
another subjective consideration
that I think is very important.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.630
And, uh, it, as in any language
learning situation, you

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:10.739
have to take the initiative.

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:15.540
You have to take the initiative to go out
there and find content of interest and

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.010
pursue things that are of interest to you.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.440
So those are some of the subjective
considerations, but there is one

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.460
factor that's kind of a combination
of subjective and objective.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:32.280
So rather than saying language X is
the most difficult or the easiest

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.970
to a large extent, it depends on
the languages you already know.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.290
So, because to me, vocabulary
is the biggest issue.

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.630
Language learning is about learning words.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.490
So if you speak a language, say you speak
Spanish and you want to learn Italian,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:53.395
obviously 85% of the words in Italian
are identifiable as being similar to

00:02:53.395 --> 00:02:58.375
Spanish, even allowing for the odd false
friend, which really doesn't matter.

00:02:58.375 --> 00:02:59.395
There aren't so many of them.

00:02:59.695 --> 00:03:04.645
The fact that the vocabulary is similar
is going to help you, uh, similarly for

00:03:04.645 --> 00:03:09.625
an English speaker, Spanish, French, all
of the Latin based languages have a lot

00:03:09.625 --> 00:03:12.055
of vocabulary in common with English.

00:03:12.295 --> 00:03:15.535
So I think the vocabulary
is the biggest issue.

00:03:15.715 --> 00:03:18.615
It's a bigger issue,
I think, than grammar.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:22.440
Because we can get used to the grammar
in time, we'll get used to the grammar,

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.850
but if we have to learn and relearn
and forget and relearn, and, and

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:31.620
there's so many words to learn that
makes the language more difficult.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:37.170
For example, Romanian has a grammatical
structure that's quite unique.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.850
They have a number of unique features.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:46.635
However, 70% of their vocabulary is
very similar to other romance languages.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:51.375
And so with that, Romanian becomes
quite easy to learn despite its

00:03:51.404 --> 00:03:53.415
different grammatical structure.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:57.795
So is the vocabulary in the
language you want to learn similar

00:03:57.795 --> 00:03:59.295
to a language you already know?

00:03:59.565 --> 00:04:02.415
So that means that for
example, for a person who...

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.340
so say a Japanese speaker.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.180
They've got the characters in Japanese
and they've got a lot of the vocabulary.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:13.440
Even the Koreans who don't use
Chinese characters, a lot of their

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.779
vocabulary, 50% just as the case with
the Japanese is of Chinese origin.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:24.180
So they have an easier time, whereas
say Europeans or people from north

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.060
America or from the Middle East,
or from somewhere else where they

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.210
don't have this vocabulary, it's
going to be more difficult for them.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:35.099
Now, objective consideration is
things like the writing system.

00:04:35.159 --> 00:04:39.480
Obviously, if it's, it it's much
easier to learn a language that's

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:43.140
written in your own writing system,
because since you were a child you've

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.580
been reading in that writing system.

00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:48.120
So to get the brain, even if you
understand how Chinese characters

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.680
work or Arabic writing, uh, it's
going to be difficult to get used

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.750
to reading, uh, comfortably quickly.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:55.620
So that...

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.849
since reading is such a big part of
language learning, if you can't read

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:01.390
comfortably, it's going to slow you down.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.705
So that's an objective consideration.

00:05:04.155 --> 00:05:07.875
Now of the different writing systems,
some of them are very much parallel

00:05:07.905 --> 00:05:11.325
to the Latin alphabet and that's the
case with Cyrillic or with Greek,

00:05:11.685 --> 00:05:16.095
others are true alphabets, like
the Hangul, but very different.

00:05:16.665 --> 00:05:20.775
And then you have syllabary is like
Japanese hiragana and Katakana.

00:05:20.865 --> 00:05:24.405
And then you have, uh, I should
point out by the way, the Arabic

00:05:24.405 --> 00:05:27.885
script is also an alphabet, but it's
for me, difficult to get used to.

00:05:28.605 --> 00:05:32.415
Um, and then you have Chinese characters,
which are even more difficult.

00:05:32.415 --> 00:05:34.935
So writing system is a big consideration.

00:05:35.385 --> 00:05:38.385
Another, um, objective
consideration is grammar.

00:05:38.745 --> 00:05:44.265
I find that of the languages that I
have learned, the Slavic languages

00:05:44.265 --> 00:05:49.155
have the most complicated grammar,
more case endings to try to remember

00:05:49.155 --> 00:05:54.705
while you're speaking, uh, certain
concepts like, uh, aspects of

00:05:54.705 --> 00:05:56.685
verbs, verbs of motion that I found.

00:05:57.405 --> 00:06:01.665
But I have never had to struggle
with issues in English like articles.

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:06.315
So maybe for speakers of those
other languages, the articles

00:06:06.315 --> 00:06:09.555
in English, and maybe some other
things, make English difficult.

00:06:09.765 --> 00:06:13.215
So it again gets back to this
idea that certain languages are

00:06:13.455 --> 00:06:15.945
subjectively easier or difficult.

00:06:16.935 --> 00:06:20.215
I know that the Foreign Service
Institute in the United States has

00:06:20.215 --> 00:06:24.180
put, you know, their evaluation of
how many instructional hours are

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:25.710
required for different languages.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:29.100
And on that basis, they rated
them by level of difficulty.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:33.930
But that's typically based on an
English speaker in a classroom.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:39.750
So how relevant that is to anybody
out there who doesn't happen to be

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.890
an English speaker studying in a
classroom I don't know, but it's also

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.805
a bit of an indicator of the level
of difficulty of different languages.

00:06:48.164 --> 00:06:52.604
So easiest to learn, I would say
for an English speaker is Spanish.

00:06:53.115 --> 00:06:58.905
Um, German is somewhat more complicated
in its grammar and I haven't done a

00:06:58.905 --> 00:07:02.715
study, but I have the feeling that the
vocabulary between English and Spanish

00:07:02.895 --> 00:07:05.265
is more similar than English and German.

00:07:05.325 --> 00:07:08.414
Although there's a lot of
vocabulary in German that helps us.

00:07:08.715 --> 00:07:12.914
I don't think either of those languages
is nearly as difficult as languages where

00:07:12.914 --> 00:07:19.275
we have no common vocabulary: Arabic,
Persian or, uh, obviously Chinese.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.165
So I hope that's helpful.

00:07:21.285 --> 00:07:25.335
And a little bit of a discussion on
the difficulty of different languages.

00:07:25.605 --> 00:07:28.395
And I'll leave you the couple of
videos I've done on the same subject.

